1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:02,800
Your exosome serum may not
contain what you think

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,120
it does.

3
00:00:04,210 --> 00:00:08,550
Exosomes are microscopic packages that
cells use to carry signals.

4
00:00:08,650 --> 00:00:11,580
But in skincare, the word
exosome isn't a complete

5
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,200
ingredient identity.

6
00:00:13,290 --> 00:00:15,960
Brands may use it
for cell-derived exosomes,

7
00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:20,830
plant extracellular vesicles, or fermentation-derived vesicles.

8
00:00:20,930 --> 00:00:22,800
These are different materials.

9
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:26,640
And evidence for one doesn't
automatically prove the others work.

10
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:29,920
And cell-derived isn't one thing either.

11
00:00:30,010 --> 00:00:33,550
Published work uses vesicles
from stem cells,

12
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:36,240
from platelets, even from milk.

13
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:37,710
There's another problem.

14
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:40,930
Much of the clinical work
pairs exosomes with microneedling

15
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:44,390
or laser, devices used precisely
to get past the barrier.

16
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:46,980
That doesn't prove a daily
serum works the same

17
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
way on intact skin.

18
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,900
Before trusting the claim,

19
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:52,560
ask three questions.

20
00:00:52,650 --> 00:00:54,240
What is the source?

21
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:56,720
Was the finished formula
tested on humans?

22
00:00:56,810 --> 00:00:59,360
And was it tested
on intact skin?

23
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:00,830
The biology is promising.

24
00:01:00,970 --> 00:01:03,080
The evidence is still developing.

25
00:01:03,170 --> 00:01:05,850
And the word exosome on
the label is not

26
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:06,880
the whole answer.
